  version: 1
}

vars:pre-request {
  adminEmail: admin@aip.com
  adminPassword: admin
  providerId: replace-with-provider-id
  locale: en
  legalPageKey: 1
}

docs {
# Rose API Collection

Use the `Local` environment for application requests. Its `baseUrl` already includes `/api`, so application URLs begin with `/app`.

## App request sequences

Customer registration is: **Register Request OTP** → **Register Verify OTP** → **Register Update Location**. Each response replaces `customerSessionToken`; the final step captures `customerAccessToken`. For an existing customer, use **Login Request OTP** → **Login Verify OTP** instead. **Resend OTP** is valid only while the current customer session represents the register or login OTP flow.

Provider registration is: **Get Categories** → **Register Request OTP** → **Register Verify OTP** → **Register Upload Documents**. The category request captures the first active `specialtyId`; registration requires at least one unique, active category and three image files. Registration ends in pending status and does not issue a bearer token. For an active provider, use **Login Request OTP** → **Login Verify OTP**; the successful login captures `providerAccessToken`. **Resend OTP** is valid only while a provider register or login OTP session is active.

All OTP examples use `123456`, which the local API accepts for development. Request/response scripts keep customer and provider session, OTP, and bearer-token variables separate.

The Local fallbacks use the currently seeded category, service, service-area, and replyable-review IDs. List/create responses refresh `specialtyId`, `serviceId`, `serviceAreaId`, and `reviewId` dynamically. Replace an ID if your local database has been reseeded.

Customer review creation requires a bearer token and a completed booking owned by that customer which has not already been reviewed. Provider replies require a bearer token for the provider who owns that review and can be submitted only once.

## Current app enums

| Field | Values |
| --- | --- |
| `locale` | `en`, `ar` |
| customer/provider `gender` | `1` male, `2` female, `3` other |
| service `gender` | `0` both, `1` men, `2` women |
| legal `pageKey` (customer) | `1` terms, `2` privacy, `3` cookie |
| legal `pageKey` (provider) | customer values plus `4` provider agreement |
| provider explore `sortBy` | `topRated`, `nearest`, `mostReviewed` |
| availability `bufferMinutes` | `15`, `30`, `45`, `60` |

Availability updates must include each of `monday` through `sunday` exactly once. Times use 24-hour `HH:mm`; enabled days require a start and end time with the end later than the start, while disabled days may use `null` times.
}
